„­bible_version£KJV¤book.§chapter¨sections–…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¦Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, unto the church of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints which are in all Achaia:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNgrace be to you and peace from God our Father, and from the Lord Jesus Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlBlessed be God, even the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies, and the God of all comfort;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£who comforteth us in all our tribulation, that we may be able to comfort them which are in any trouble, by the comfort wherewith we ourselves are comforted of God.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZFor as the sufferings of Christ abound in us, so our consolation also aboundeth by Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÜAnd whether we be afflicted, it is for your consolation and salvation, which is effectual in the enduring of the same sufferings which we also suffer: or whether we be comforted, it is for your consolation and salvation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}And our hope of you is stedfast, knowing, that as ye are partakers of the sufferings, so shall ye be also of the consolation.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´For we would not, brethren, have you ignorant of our trouble which came to us in Asia, that we were pressed out of measure, above strength, insomuch that we despaired even of life:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxbut we had the sentence of death in ourselves, that we should not trust in ourselves, but in God which raiseth the dead:¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
