„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•ye also helping together by prayer for us, that for the gift bestowed upon us by the means of many persons thanks may be given by many on our behalf.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙáFor our rejoicing is this, the testimony of our conscience, that in simplicity and godly sincerity, not with fleshly wisdom, but by the grace of God, we have had our conversation in the world, and more abundantly to you-ward.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|For we write none other things unto you, than what ye read or acknowledge; and I trust ye shall acknowledge even to the end;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|as also ye have acknowledged us in part, that we are your rejoicing, even as ye also are our's in the day of the Lord Jesus.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd in this confidence I was minded to come unto you before, that ye might have a second benefit;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand to pass by you into Macedonia, and to come again out of Macedonia unto you, and of you to be brought on my way toward JudÃ¦a.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬When I therefore was thus minded, did I use lightness? or the things that I purpose, do I purpose according to the flesh, that with me there should be yea yea, and nay nay?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<But as God is true, our word toward you was not yea and nay.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was preached among you by us, even by me and Silvanus and Timotheus, was not yea and nay, but in him was yea.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYFor all the promises of God in him are yea, and in him Amen, unto the glory of God by us.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMNow he which stablisheth us with you in Christ, and hath anointed us, is God;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKwho hath also sealed us, and given the earnest of the Spirit in our hearts.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Moreover I call God for a record upon my soul, that to spare you I came not as yet unto Corinth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbNot for that we have dominion over your faith, but are helpers of your joy: for by faith ye stand.¦layout ªlast_verse